    "description": "Artist Unknown\nStanding Man with Pipe and Sickle\nHand-Carved Solid Wood Sculpture\n28\" x 5\" x 5\"\nUnsigned\nThis striking figurative wood carving reflects traditional African folk art sculpture, carved from a single piece of solid hardwood. The tall, elongated composition depicts a standing male figure smoking a long pipe while holding a curved sickle or tapping knife, with a textured cross-body pouch draped over his right shoulder. The artisan has rendered expressive facial contours, prominent eyes, textured hair, and incised hatching along the shirt and pouch, set atop an integral cylindrical base.\nCarved from a single log of natural wood with visible tool marks and grain patterns\nDetailed relief carving on the woven-style pouch and rolled pant leg cuff\nTraditional folk art representation of agrarian harvest or palm wine tapping\nCondition:\nVery good vintage condition with an attractive aged wood patina. Features natural age checks, wood grain separations, and minor surface wear consistent with age and hand craftsmanship. Structurally sound and stands firmly upright.\nTHANK YOU FOR SUPPORTING OUR MISSION!\nIf there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to respond to all inquiries within 2 business days.\nOur business hours are Monday - Friday  7:00 am to 3:00 pm EST\n**If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so.\n**Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nGoodwill of Western and Northern Connecticut strengthens communities by helping people with disabilities and other disadvantages maximize independence through job training and other support services.",
